---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { pages } from '../lib/registry';
---

<Page
  {...pages['/experience/']}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Start', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Experience', href: '/experience/' },
  ]}
>
  <header class="page-intro wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">For collaborators and hiring teams</p>
    <h1>Engineering judgment, made visible.</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      Public work offers a concrete way to discuss software, data, visualisation
      and technical communication.
    </p>
  </header>
  <article class="reading">
    <h2>Software and interfaces</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/work/#shiny-filters">Shiny-filteRs</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/work/#hinuhinu">Hinuhinu</a> connect computation and visual
      interfaces. <a href="/work/#puttpulse">PuttPulse</a> brings a product
      perspective to disc-golf practice.
    </p>
    <h2>Data and reproducibility</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/writing/fitbit-gamification/">Fitbit API article</a>,{' '}
      <a href="/writing/supervised-umap/">UMAP slideshow</a> and writing on{' '}
      <a href="/writing/drake/">Drake</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/writing/rprofile/">.Rprofile automation</a> show implementation
      steps rather than only finished images.
    </p>
    <h2>Communication</h2>
    <p>
      Articles and presentations explain methods, examples and technical
      choices. Original dates and source material remain attached so historical
      work can be read in context.
    </p>
    <h2>Discuss a role</h2>
    <p>
      For full-time opportunities, contact me for a current CV and a discussion
      of relevant responsibilities. The old site's résumé is retained as
      historical material, not presented as a verified current employment
      record.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="/contact/">
      Discuss an opportunity ↗
    </a>
  </article>
</Page>
